# Terms blog-craft's writing-standard checker accepts in super-fr's published
# docs (scripts/check-writing-standards.sh; spec 2026-11-13-writing-standards-docs
# R4). One term per line. List a term only when a standard would otherwise flag
# a word the page cannot avoid; never to silence a sentence that should change.

# Abbreviations that are the name readers know the thing by, in prose, commands
# and UI labels alike. Spelling them out at first use would name something the
# reader then has to translate back.
API
CI
CLI
HEAD
HTML
ID
JSON
PATH
PR
README
REST
SSH
UI
URL
YAML

# fr nouns that end in -ing. Each names a thing (a journal entry kind, a check
# severity, a status, a page layout, a skill), not an action, so no verb can
# replace it.
debugging
finding
landing
pending
sibling
warning
